.\" man/man3/Docv::Term::Tty.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Term::Tty" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Term::Tty \- The controlling terminal: raw mode, size, and entering/leaving the full\-screen state with all input reporting.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Term::Tty\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The controlling terminal: raw mode, size, and entering/leaving the
full\-screen state with all input reporting.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.PP
\fBTIOCGWINSZ = 21523_u64\fR
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(input : IO::FileDescriptor = STDIN, output : IO::FileDescriptor = STDOUT)\fR
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.color_depth(no_color : String | Nil = ENV["NO_COLOR"]?, colorterm : String | Nil = ENV["COLORTERM"]?, term : String | Nil = ENV["TERM"]?) : ColorDepth\fR
The color depth the environment announces: none when \fIno_color\fR
(\fB\%NO_COLOR\fR) is set and not empty, 24\-bit when \fIcolorterm\fR is
\fB\%truecolor\fR or \fB\%24bit\fR, 256 colors when \fIterm\fR names a \fB\%256color\fR or
\fB\%direct\fR terminal, the 16 ANSI colors otherwise. A terminal that
answers the OSC 21 query (\fB\%Sequences::COLORS_QUERY\fR) shows 24\-bit color
whatever this says.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef copy(text : String) : Nil\fR
Puts \fItext\fR on the system clipboard (OSC 52).
.TP 4
\fBdef enter : Nil\fR
Enters the alternate screen, pushes the keyboard mode inside it, and
enables mouse and notification reporting.
.PP
\fBdef input : IO::FileDescriptor\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef leave : Nil\fR
Undoes \fB\%enter\fR in reverse order, resetting the pointer shape.
.PP
\fBdef output : IO::FileDescriptor\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef pointer(shape : String) : Nil\fR
Sets the mouse pointer to the CSS cursor \fIshape\fR (\fB\%pointer\fR, \fB\%text\fR,
\fB\%ew\-resize\fR ...; OSC 22); an empty shape resets it.
.TP 4
\fBdef query_colors : Nil\fR
Asks the terminal for its theme colors again (after a color scheme
change).
.TP 4
\fBdef raw : Nil\fR
Switches the input to raw mode, remembering the previous settings.
.TP 4
\fBdef restore : Nil\fR
Restores the settings saved by \fB\%raw\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef size : Tuple(Int32, Int32, Int32, Int32)\fR
The window size: rows, columns, pixel width, pixel height.
.TP 4
\fBdef tty? : Bool\fR
True when both ends are terminals.
.TP 4
\fBdef write(data : String | Bytes) : Nil\fR
Writes \fIdata\fR and flushes.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/term/tty.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv::Term" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Term::Sequences" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
